+---
+id: PLAN-012-vtt-session-export
+status: draft
+date: 2026-11-05
+review_count: 0
+patch: n/a
+---
+
+# PLAN-012: WebVTT export endpoint for stored session transcripts
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Governing records
+
+- BDR-006: the canonical transcript artifact is a standard subtitle file
+  (`<stem>.srt`) chosen so transcripts are usable outside the app. An
+  HTTP export that derives a second standard subtitle format extends the
+  same rationale without changing canonical storage.
+- ADR-007: the `.srt` file is the single source of truth for the
+  transcript, and `readSession` already returns its raw text as
+  `StoredSession.srt`. ADR-007 rejected WebVTT as the *storage* format;
+  this plan does not contradict it - VTT is produced by conversion at
+  request time and is never written to disk or stored.
+- ADR-006: no new dependencies. The SRT -> VTT conversion is a small
+  pure function written by hand, same policy as the hand-rolled SRT
+  helpers in `server/session/srt.ts`.
+- BDR-002: zero added runtime cost and zero new dependencies.
+- ADR-001: local single-user Fastify app; the endpoint joins the
+  existing `registerSessionRoutes` REST surface, no auth, no new
+  infrastructure.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. A pure `srtToVtt` conversion function in a new
+   `server/session/vtt.ts` module.
+2. `GET /api/sessions/:id/export?format=vtt` in
+   `server/session/routes.ts`: 200 + WebVTT body, 404 for unknown
+   session, 400 for unsupported or missing `format`.
+3. Automated tests: `server/session/vtt.test.ts` (unit) plus endpoint
+   cases in `server/app.test.ts` (happy path, 404, 400).
+
+Out of scope: any web client download UI (a Review/Sessions download
+button is a follow-up), new export formats (`format` is an enum for
+future formats but only `vtt` is implemented), WebVTT features beyond
+the cue mapping (`<v Speaker>` voice tags, `NOTE` metadata,
+`X-TIMESTAMP-MAP`), and changes to storage, writers, or the `.md`/`.wav`
+artifacts.
+
+## Contracts (literal)
+
+Route added inside `registerSessionRoutes`
+(`server/session/routes.ts`):
+
+```ts
+const exportQuerySchema = z.object({ format: z.literal('vtt') });
+
+app.get('/api/sessions/:id/export', async (req, reply) => {
+  const { id } = req.params as { id: string };
+  const stored = await readSession(sessions.dir, id);
+  if (!stored) {
+    return reply.code(404).send({ error: `session not found: ${id}` });
+  }
+  const { format: _format } = exportQuerySchema.parse(req.query ?? {});
+  return reply
+    .header('Content-Type', 'text/vtt')
+    .header('Content-Disposition', `attachment; filename="${id}.vtt"`)
+    .send(srtToVtt(stored.srt));
+});
+```
+
+- Ordering is pinned: the session is resolved first, then the query is
+  validated. Unknown id returns 404 regardless of `format`; a known id
+  with `format` missing or anything other than `vtt` throws `ZodError`,
+  which the existing `setErrorHandler` in `server/index.ts` maps to
+  `400 { error: 'invalid request', issues: [...] }`.
+- Response headers: `Content-Type: text/vtt` (the IANA-registered type
+  for WebVTT) and `Content-Disposition: attachment;
+  filename="<session-id>.vtt"` where `<session-id>` is the `:id` path
+  parameter (e.g. `2026-11-05-session-1026.vtt`). Session ids are
+  restricted to `[a-z0-9-]` plus the `YYYY-MM-DD` day prefix, so the
+  header value needs no escaping.
+- `readSession` is reused as-is: it gives the same 404 semantics as
+  `GET /api/sessions/:id` and `GET /api/sessions/:id/audio` (invalid id
+  shape or missing `.md` -> null -> 404). A session whose `.srt` is
+  missing or empty exports a header-only `WEBVTT` document, which is
+  valid WebVTT.
+
+Conversion function (`server/session/vtt.ts`):
+
+```ts
+export function srtToVtt(srt: string): string
+```
+
+Behavior, pinned:
+
+- Output is `WEBVTT\n\n` followed by the converted cue body. Input that
+  is empty or whitespace-only yields `WEBVTT\n` (a bare valid header).
+- Conversion is line-based: any line containing ` --> ` has every `,`
+  replaced by `.` (SRT `HH:MM:SS,mmm` -> WebVTT `HH:MM:SS.mmm`). All
+  other lines pass through byte-for-byte: cue numbers remain as WebVTT
+  cue identifiers (legal per spec, preserving the `segment index + 1`
+  binding from ADR-007), and cue text lines keep the exact source and
+  translation text, including the optional `Speaker: ` prefix.
+- No re-parsing into cues and no re-formatting of numbers: the stored
+  `.srt` is already machine-written, so a line transform is sufficient
+  and keeps the converter to roughly ten lines.
+
+Resulting body for the ADR-007 example:
+
+```
+WEBVTT
+
+1
+00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.800
+Speaker 1: Hello.
+Xin chào.
+
+2
+00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.200
+Hi there.
+```
+
+## Steps
+
+1. `server/session/vtt.ts` (new): `srtToVtt` per the pinned contract.
+   Comment style matches `srt.ts` (one short block explaining the
+   line-transform rule and the identifier passthrough).
+2. `server/session/routes.ts`: import `srtToVtt`, add
+   `exportQuerySchema` beside the other schemas, and register the
+   `GET /api/sessions/:id/export` handler next to
+   `GET /api/sessions/:id`, using the exact handler body pinned above
+   (header style matches the audio route's `.header(...)` calls).
+3. `server/session/vtt.test.ts` (new): unit tests for `srtToVtt`.
+4. `server/app.test.ts`: new `describe('session export')` block with the
+   three endpoint cases. The fixture writes session files directly into
+   the tmp `dir` (`renderFrontmatter` + a small `.srt` string), which is
+   cheaper than driving the WS flow and does not depend on
+   `FakeProvider`; `readSession` only needs the `.md` + `.srt` pair.
+5. Commit, then log via `CONTEXTS/04-logs/event.py`.
+
+## Test plan
+
+`server/session/vtt.test.ts`:
+
+- converts a two-cue bilingual SRT into `WEBVTT` + blank line + cues
+  with `.`-separated timestamps; cue numbers and both text lines pass
+  through unchanged.
+- single-line cue (no translation yet) stays single-line.
+- commas inside cue text are NOT touched (only ` --> ` lines convert).
+- empty string and whitespace-only input return `WEBVTT\n`.
+
+`server/app.test.ts` (`describe('session export')`):
+
+- happy path: seed `dir` with a `.md` (via `renderFrontmatter`) +
+  `.srt`, then `app.inject({ method: 'GET', url:
+  '/api/sessions/<id>/export?format=vtt' })`. Assert `statusCode` 200,
+  `content-type` contains `text/vtt`, `content-disposition` matches
+  `attachment; filename="<id>.vtt"`, body starts with `WEBVTT\n`, the
+  cue timing line uses `.` separators and no `,` remains in it, and the
+  text lines equal the seeded `.srt` text lines.
+- unknown session id -> 404.
+- `format=json` and missing `format` -> 400 (the `ZodError` path).
+
+Gates: `npm run typecheck` and `npm test` (vitest) green.
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- Assumption (task skipped clarification): "match what the existing SRT
+  export contains" is read as the stored `.srt` artifact returned by
+  `readSession` - there is no existing SRT HTTP endpoint. Content parity
+  is therefore guaranteed by line passthrough.
+- Assumption: `format` is required and only `vtt` is accepted; a missing
+  value is a 400. If a default export format is ever wanted, the schema
+  grows a `.default('vtt')` - not pinned now.
+- Assumption: check order is session-then-format, so a request that is
+  both an unknown id and a bad format returns 404, matching the
+  `/audio` route's session-first resolution.
+- Cue text containing a literal `-->` would be ambiguous in the stored
+  `.srt` already (`cueCount` counts ` --> ` lines); the converter keeps
+  such text byte-for-byte for content parity. STT output does not
+  produce this in practice; noted, not handled.
+- WebVTT cue payload must not contain `-->` per strict parsers; see
+  previous note - accepted edge case for content parity.
+- `Content-Type: text/vtt` is the registered type; some players also
+  accept `text/vtt;charset=utf-8` - not pinned since the body is
+  download-oriented, not streamed to a `<track>` element.
+- Follow-up (not this plan): a download button in Review or Sessions,
+  and possibly `format=srt` as a passthrough alias if clients ever want
+  the stored file over HTTP.
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `server/session/vtt.ts` exports `srtToVtt` per the pinned
+      contract; `GET /api/sessions/:id/export?format=vtt` serves valid
+      WebVTT with `text/vtt` and an attachment `Content-Disposition`.
+- [ ] Unknown session id returns 404; missing or non-`vtt` `format`
+      returns 400.
+- [ ] New unit tests plus the three `app.test.ts` endpoint cases pass;
+      `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` are green.
+- [ ] No new dependencies; no changes to storage, writers, or web code.
+- [ ] Code committed; completion event logged via `event.py`; DoD items
+      ticked and plan status set to `implemented`.
-- 
